<h2>do talk to scholars in your field that you know about from the literature</h2>

<dl>
  <li> The scholars in your narrowly defined field will not be at your school. 
    There is a handful of them, say 5-50, and they are scattered around the
    world--email them, they would be happy. 
  <li> You are both passionate about the same thing. Coauthor! Most scholars
    need coauthors and would like to have a new one. Ideally get a junior scholar
    to team up: PhD student or assistant professor, they are more upto
    date, more eager, and more in need to do research. 
  <li> Can also try a well established senior scholar (published a lot
    and cited a lot), but make sure she is still productive (still is
    publishing recently in good reputable outlets).
    But avoid top top scholars like Nobel prize winners, they will not talk to you.
</dl>
